  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1948 near Aztec, New Mexico, a man named Solon Brown broke down and cried while telling a church deacon named Bruce Seer about what he had seen, in the setting of a reported saucer crash there. Michels tells it in an episode about that crash, drawing on the researcher Scott Ramsey. Sixty years later, Seer's son told Ramsey he never forgot that night, because it was the first time he had ever seen a grown man cry."
